[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/comments/301112020","html_url":"https://github.com/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/3000#issuecomment-301112020","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/3000","id":301112020,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMwMTExMjAyMA==","user":{"login":"kchodorow","id":17042,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MDQy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17042?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kchodorow","html_url":"https://github.com/kchodorow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kchodorow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kchodorow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kchodorow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kchodorow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kchodorow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kchodorow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kchodorow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kchodorow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kchodorow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2017-05-12T15:42:17Z","updated_at":"2017-05-12T15:42:17Z","body":"I'm actually not sure why it doesn't pick this up automatically, but it seems to only be looking for crosstools in `@local_config_cc`, which doesn't contain a ppc crosstool (?).  You have to give the `--crosstool_top=//tools/cpp:default-toolchain` argument to make it look at //tools/cpp, which _does_ contain a ppc toolchain.\r\n\r\nHowever, I'm not actually sure how to give extra arguments to the ./compile.sh script, so assigning to @damienmg for clarification on:\r\n\r\n1. How to pass `--crosstool_top` into `./compile.sh`.\r\n2. Why `@local_config_cc` doesn't contain the same toolchain as `@bazel_tools`.\r\n3. Why they aren't both used to find toolchains.","author_a